<p>I gave a presentation at Macstock X that I thought people might be interested in. It was about Markdown publishing, and ostensibly about Marked, although I didn&rsquo;t get to as much about Marked as I had intended. It still went pretty well.</p>

<p>I created the whole presentation in Markdown and presented it with Reveal.js, using Multiplex so people could follow along on their own machines, able to follow links, bookmark slides, copy code blocks, etc. People really seemed to enjoy that aspect of it.</p>

<p>So I&rsquo;m making the presentation available, including speaker notes. <a href="https://brettterpstra.com/macstock2026/slideshow.html">View it on the web</a> and you&rsquo;ll be able to navigate the slide show. Press <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">O</code> to see an overview and navigate quickly, and press <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">S</code> to see the speaker view. Additionally, <a href="https://brettterpstra.com/macstock2026/slides.md">the source for the presentation is available in Markdown</a>. It has some special formatting for Reveal.js, but is totally readable.</p>

<p>I tend to tell bad jokes when I&rsquo;m nervous, so there are plenty included in the deck. My apologies in advance.</p>

